</div>

<div class=3D"mainbox" id=3D"introblurb">
<p>The LMS-EPSRC Durham Research Symposia began in 1974 and have now become=
 an established and <a href=3D"http://www.ams.org/notices/200111/comm-durha=
msympos.pdf">recognised</a> series of international research meetings, havi=
ng celebrated its 100th symposium.
They provide an excellent opportunity to explore an area of research in dep=
th, to learn of new developments, and to instigate links between different =
branches.
The format is designed to allow substantial time for interaction and resear=
ch.
The meetings, by invitation only, are usually held in July and August, and =
usually lasting for 10 days with up to 70 participants, roughly half of who=
m will come from the UK.
Lectures and seminars take place in the Durham campus and participants are =
housed in en-suite accommodation at a Durham college.</p>

<p>Details about how to make a proposal can be accessed directly from the <=
a href=3D"http://www.lms.ac.uk/">LMS</a>.
The <a href=3D"http://www.epsrc.ac.uk/">EPSRC</a> is the main funder of the=
 symposia.</p>

<p>The list of the meetings (most recent first) follows, including the main=
 webpage, as well as direct links to the list of participants, the programm=
e, movies of the talks and conference photograph where available.</p>
<br>
</div>

